# Novopay remote QA / UAT / preprod

## Autofetch credentials (do not ask the user to paste)

**Single source of truth:** `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\novopay-remote-db.env`  
(Windows: `C:\Users\ashutosh.kumar\.cursor\novopay-remote-db.env`)

Key-name template only: `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\novopay-remote-db.env.example`

Whenever QA / UAT / preprod DB, SSH, applogs, or Flyway verify is needed: **load that env file via the helpers below**. Do not ask Ashutosh for hosts, users, passwords, or keys if the file is filled. Never print secret values. If a required key is empty, name the missing key and stop.

| Need | Env keys (prefix `QA_` / `UAT_` / `PREPROD_`) | Helper |
| --- | --- | --- |
| MySQL | `{ENV}_DB_HOST`, `{ENV}_DB_PORT`, `{ENV}_DB_USER`, `{ENV}_DB_PASSWORD`, `{ENV}_DB_SCHEMA`, `{ENV}_DB_VIA_SSH` | `novopay-remote-db-readonly.py --env qa\|uat\|preprod` |
| App server SSH / applogs | `{ENV}_SSH_HOST`, `{ENV}_SSH_PORT`, `{ENV}_SSH_USER`, `{ENV}_SSH_KEY` **or** `{ENV}_SSH_PASSWORD`, optional `{ENV}_SSH_JUMP_*` | `novopay-remote-ssh.py --env qa\|uat\|preprod` |
| Superset (QA / UAT) | `{ENV}_SUPERSET_URL`, `{ENV}_SUPERSET_USER`, `{ENV}_SUPERSET_PASSWORD` | `novopay-superset-readonly.py --env qa\|uat` (login + GET only; `--get <path>`, `--find-sql <text>`) |

Same file holds DB, app-server SSH and Superset. There is no separate SSH-only or Superset-only env file.

## Superset servers

- QA: `https://ddp-qa-superset.trustt.com` - metadata in QA MySQL `ddp_superset` (`tables` = datasets, `slices` = charts, `dashboards`, `dashboard_roles`).
- UAT: `https://ddp-uat-superset.trustt.com` - **same instance as QA** (verified 2026-10-05: identical DB connections and datasets). UAT MySQL `ddp_superset` is a separate stale copy - trust the API / QA `ddp_superset`.
- Prod DDP: `https://ddp-superset.novopay.in` (no access). Prod DSA Superset URL is set manually, not via Flyway.
- In Git Bash, prefix `--get` paths with `//` (e.g. `//api/v1/dashboard/1`) to stop MSYS path rewriting.
- Not on the QA app box (no superset process there). Admin portal reads `superset.base.url` from `{tenant}_masterdata.configuration`.
- Admin portal reports (UAM population / activity, DSA dashboards) are Superset virtual datasets, not code. Inspect via `ddp_superset` SELECTs or Superset API GETs.
- **Read-only always:** never create/edit/delete datasets, charts, dashboards, roles, or run write SQL in SQL Lab - even with admin creds. Same ask-first rule as DB writes.

Typical QA mapping (values live in the env file, not here): `QA_DB_*` for MySQL; `QA_SSH_*` for the Linux app box used for `/apps/applogs` greps.

## Default - read-only

QA and preprod DB users **have write grants**. That does not authorize writes by default.

- Default: SELECT / SHOW / DESCRIBE / EXPLAIN / WITH only via `novopay-remote-db-readonly.py`.
- Do not fix data, run Flyway, or create temp tables on your own.
- If a task needs a write, **stop and show the exact SQL first**. Do not run it yet.

## Writes - only when the user asks first

**Never run any INSERT / UPDATE / DELETE / REPLACE / DDL / GRANT / LOAD / CALL / SET GLOBAL on QA, UAT, or preprod unless the user explicitly asked to run that statement** (after seeing the query, or by saying seed/run/execute this SQL).

- Run only the approved statement. Do not add sibling writes in the same turn.
- Do not keep a general write helper. The readonly script stays the default; bypass READ ONLY only for the asked statement.
- After a write, verify with SELECT and report the row. Do not print passwords.

## When to use

For RCA, env drift, "what is on QA/UAT/preprod", Flyway verify, or any analysis that needs live data: **run SELECT / log greps yourself**. Do not ask the user to paste query or grep results if this file is filled in.

## How

```
python %USERPROFILE%\.cursor\novopay-remote-db-readonly.py --env qa      --sql "SELECT 1"
python %USERPROFILE%\.cursor\novopay-remote-db-readonly.py --env uat     --sql "SHOW DATABASES"
python %USERPROFILE%\.cursor\novopay-remote-db-readonly.py --env preprod --ping
python %USERPROFILE%\.cursor\novopay-remote-ssh.py --env qa      --cmd "hostname; whoami"
python %USERPROFILE%\.cursor\novopay-remote-ssh.py --env preprod --cmd "ls /apps/applogs"
```

`--env qa` / `--env uat` / `--env preprod`. SQL must be one statement: `SELECT` / `SHOW` / `DESCRIBE` / `EXPLAIN` / `WITH`. The helper refuses writes.

## Rules

- Fully qualified `schema_name.table_name`.
- If a key in the env file is empty, tell the user which key to fill. Do not invent hosts or passwords.
- Write grants on the DB user are not blanket permission. Ask first, then run only that statement.
